  "scenario": "Boot the board-specific kernel with the established Zero 4 graphics DTB and stock Plasma. Verify the timer, ordinary native KMS and Qt Quick Vulkan output. Confirm reference NPU compute, GPU IRQ status and Ethernet.",
  "expected": "Observe kern.clockrate at 1000 Hz and a working stock Wayland desktop. Complete 2000 CPU-filled KMS flips near one field per update and run both Qt scenes. Verify the NPU output and test data integrity on Ethernet and Wi-Fi.",
  "observed": "The board reported 1000 Hz. The native test completed 2000 flips in 33.463 seconds with three skipped fields. Stock Plasma resumed. The steady Qt scene gave 1989 swaps and the resize scene gave 2544 swaps, each over 60 seconds. The observers counted 1109 and 1368 framebuffer changes over 2000 consecutive intervals per scene. The NPU matched 24 reference frames. The wired gigabit and Wi-Fi paths delivered matching 4 MiB test transfers. DRM, display engine and GPU IRQ fault counts stayed at zero.",
